  "text": "12.6 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 63 milligrams, which is fairly controlled for a meat. Saturated fat is 4.36 grams though, so there is still some real baggage attached. Omega 3 is only 90 milligrams, meaning it is not bringing much of the more useful fat usually found in oily fish. For meats, the fat mix decides how cleanly the protein arrives, and pork loin lands somewhere in the middle.",
